/// A mob, as vanilla's `Mob` has it (CAL-156): a living entity (`world.living`) of a category that
/// natural spawning counts, made by its type and finalized as `finalizeSpawn` finalizes it, from
/// the level's random: what its kind draws first, then its follow range's random spawn bonus,
/// `triangle(0, 0.11485)`, and whether it's left-handed, 1 in 20. It has its own flags, without
/// AI, left-handed and aggressive; whether it must stay, `PersistenceRequired`, and may pick up
/// loot; how long it's done nothing, `noActionTime`; and now and then its ambient sound, `baseTick`'s
/// draw from its own random against how long since its last, which starts again at less its
/// interval, 80 a mob's and 120 an animal's, `getAmbientSoundInterval`.
///
/// An ageable mob, `AgeableMob`, has an age: below 0 a baby growing up a tick at a time, unless
/// its age is locked, above 0 how long until it can breed, counting down. A pack of them is
/// finalized together, each after the first a baby 1 in 20, as `AgeableMobGroupData` has it. An
/// animal, `Animal`, has its love, which its age being anything but 0 takes away.
///
/// The kinds Calcite makes are the farm animals, each with its size grown and as a baby,
/// `BABY_DIMENSIONS`, and its sounds, its steps at 0.15:
/// - the mooshroom, `MushroomCow`, 0.9 by 1.4, red or brown, mooing as a classic cow at 0.4;
/// - the cow, `Cow`, the same size, its variant drawn by where it spawns and its sound variant at
///   random, classic or moody, at 0.4;
/// - the pig, `Pig`, 0.9 by 0.9, and the chicken, `Chicken`, 0.4 by 0.7, each with its variant and
///   sound variant as a cow's, a baby's sounds its own; a chicken falls slowly, isn't hurt by
///   falling, and lays an egg of its variant every 6,000 to 12,000 ticks, drawn from its own
///   random;
/// - the sheep, `Sheep`, 0.9 by 1.3, its wool's color drawn by the climate where it spawns,
///   `SheepColorSpawnRules`;
/// - and the horse, `Horse`, and the donkey, `Donkey`, about 1.4 across, 1.6 and 1.5 high, a foal
///   0.7 and 0.5 of that, neighing every 400 ticks at least at 0.8, six of a pack at a place, each
///   with its most health drawn as it spawns, `randomizeAttributes`, and a horse its speed and
///   jump, and its variant, the pack's, and markings; each tick it draws for its tail, heals a
///   point 1 in 900, and grazes on grass 1 in 300 for 50 ticks, which its flags show.
/// - The zombie horse, `ZombieHorse`, a horse's size and steps, a monster by its category but no
///   `Monster`, allowed in peaceful and burning in daylight: spawned naturally, a zombie made and
///   finalized as its rider, holding an iron spear, before its own draws, its jump then its speed,
///   `randomizeAttributes`; a foal never grows up, `canAgeUp`; and it goes far away.
///
/// And the monsters, `Monster`, whose sounds are the hostile source's, with their swims, splashes
/// and falls the hostile's, which in light over half at their eyes do nothing three times as fast,
/// `updateNoActionTime`, and gone in peaceful (CAL-156). Each is finalized by the difficulty where
/// it spawns, `Occasion`, and most of its odds go by its special multiplier, 0 in a new world on
/// normal: after `Mob`'s draws, armor by those odds, its tier and how many pieces drawn,
/// `populateDefaultEquipmentSlots`, and a draw to enchant each slot that holds something, a
/// quarter's for the main hand and half for each armor slot by the multiplier,
/// `populateDefaultEquipmentEnchantments`; and on Halloween a pumpkin on a bare head, 1 in 4.
/// - The creeper, `Creeper`, 0.6 by 1.7, with no sound of its own and the block's steps; ignited,
///   it swells to its fuse, its primed sound as it starts.
/// - The zombie, `Zombie`, 0.6 by 1.95, its pack a baby's 1 in 20 and each a jockey's 1 in 20 then
///   1 in 20 again on a new chicken, made and finalized beside it, then whether it breaks doors, an
///   iron sword, spear or shovel 1 in 100, 1 in 20 on hard, and its attributes from its own random,
///   `handleAttributes`, its reinforcements' chance, knockback resistance, follow range and 1 in 20
///   by the multiplier a leader's; a baby 0.49 by 0.98, half as fast again. In water to its eyes
///   for 600 ticks it starts becoming a drowned, 300 more.
/// - The skeleton, `Skeleton`, 0.6 by 1.99, always holding a bow, and whether it picks up loot.
/// - The spider, `Spider`, 1.4 by 0.9: 1 in 100 a skeleton made and finalized as its rider; its
///   pack's effect drawn on hard and given it for ever (CAL-163); and climbing as it bumps into a
///   wall, which its flags show.
/// - The enderman, `Enderman`, 0.6 by 2.9, finalized by `Mob`'s draws alone, carrying nothing and
///   angry at no one, and staying where it carries a block, `requiresCustomPersistence`.
/// - The witch, `Witch`, 0.6 by 1.95, a raider, `Raider`, drawing as it's finalized for a patrol's
///   leader, which it never is, then `Mob`'s; it does nothing three times as fast in any light, and
///   each tick, not drinking, draws for each potion it might drink, then 1 in about 1,333 shows its
///   particles, entity event 15.
/// - The zombie villager, `ZombieVillager`, a zombie that doesn't drown into a drowned, its baby
///   0.49 by 0.98 with its eyes at 0.67: its profession drawn from its own random as it's made,
///   after its UUID, and its type the biome's as it's finalized, before the zombie's draws, its
///   villager data then final; it goes far away only where it's no experience and isn't being
///   cured.
///
/// The villager, `Villager` (CAL-160), an ageable mob, no animal, of the misc category, 0.6 by 1.95
/// and a baby 0.49 by 0.98, which may pick up loot and never goes far away: its brain made with its
/// sensors as it's made and again as it's read, as its age crosses into or out of being a baby,
/// and as its data's read, `refreshBrain`; its villager data, plains with no profession until it's
/// finalized, its type then the biome's; its gossip, decayed each day, a hit by a player adding
/// 25 minor negative of them and showing its anger, entity event 13; and its unhappiness, 40 ticks
/// of it and a no as a player uses a baby, or a grown one with no trades; and the player it trades
/// with, `tradingPlayer`, whose merchant menu its level opens, its ambient sound a trade's while
/// it trades, followed and looked at. Its brain's activities, trades themselves, sleeping and its
/// inventory come with CAL-160.
///
/// And the slime, `Slime`, a cube mob, `AbstractCubeMob`: an ageable mob that's never a baby and no
/// monster, its sounds the hostile source's, 0.52 across and high by its size, which is 1 as it's
/// made and 1, 2 or 4 as it spawns, drawn after `Mob`'s draws, its most health its size squared;
/// where its size changes it's turned as its head is. Landing, it draws for its particles and
/// squishes.
///
/// The zombie, zombie villager and skeleton draw each tick to burn where monsters burn and the
/// light at their eyes is over half, `isSunBurnTick`.
///
/// Each tick, before its tick, it may go, `checkDespawn`: in peaceful where its type isn't allowed
/// in it; and where it needn't stay, past its category's despawn distance from the nearest player,
/// or after 600 ticks doing nothing one in 800 past 32 blocks, where it's removed far away, which
/// no animal is. Within 32 blocks of a player, its ticks doing nothing start again.
///
/// Thinking, `serverAiStep`, it ticks its navigation, which sets its move control toward the next
/// node of its path; then its own step; then its controls, `world.navigation`'s: its move control
/// turns it and sets it walking, or a slime's turns it toward its way and hops, `CubeMobMoveControl`,
/// drawing its delay and its sound's pitch; its look control turns its head; and its jump control
/// passes on a jump. After it moves, its body turns, `BodyRotationControl`, thinking or not. Its
/// navigation is made as its constructor makes it, with its kind's maluses: an animal's beside
/// fire and in it, a chicken's and an enderman's in water; and it floats where its kind's float
/// goal would let it as it's made, all but the zombies and skeletons. A zombie that may break doors
/// may open them (CAL-157).
///
/// Its goals are its kind's, `registerGoals`, kept by `world.goals`' `GoalSelector` and run as
/// vanilla's runs them, in full each other tick by its ID, else only those that tick every tick
/// (CAL-158). A farm animal floats, `FloatGoal`; strolls, `WaterAvoidingRandomStrollGoal`, to the
/// place of the highest walk target value of those it tries, an animal's highest over grass;
/// looks at the nearest player in sight within 6, `LookAtPlayerGoal`, and around,
/// `RandomLookAroundGoal`; and a sheep eats, `EatBlockGoal`, the grass where it stands or the grass
/// block below it, its wool coming back and a baby growing a minute. A horse stands now and then,
/// `RandomStandGoal`, its ambient sound played as it does, and thinks of nothing while it stands
/// or eats, `isImmobile`, as vanilla's.
///
/// Its spawn equipment is enchanted as `enchantItemFromProvider` enchants it from
/// `mob_spawn_equipment` (D522).
///
/// Not yet: picking up loot, which its spawn only draws whether it may for; riding, so a jockey's
/// mount and rider stand apart, a chicken near isn't taken as one, and a zombie horse with its
/// rider grazes as one without, drawing for it; a creeper exploding, which waits for explosions
/// (CAL-182); a zombie's or skeleton's conversion once it comes, and a skeleton freezing in powder
/// snow, which Calcite doesn't find it in yet; a zombie villager's cure going on; and the goals
/// whose workings come later, `world.goals`' `LATER_` ones, as a witch's patrol.
module world.mob

